    <string name="sajdah_title">Sajdah verses</string>
    <string name="sajdah_header">15 verses carry a prostration marker. The Hanafi set of 14 is shown first; verses that differ by school carry a note.</string>
    <string name="sajdah_section_hanafi">Hanafi set · 14 verses</string>
    <string name="sajdah_section_other">Also marked in other schools</string>
    <string name="sajdah_note_hajj">Counted by Shafi\'i and Hanbali; not counted by Hanafis.</string>
    <string name="sajdah_note_sad">Counted by Hanafis; Shafi\'i and Hanbali treat it as a prostration of gratitude, not a recitation sajdah.</string>
    <string name="sajdah_open_hint">Tapping a verse opens its surah\'s first page — swipe forward to reach the verse. Exact verse pages are not shown for this mushaf.</string>
    <string name="sajdah_footer_schools">Maliki and Hanbali details vary between sources and are not listed here.</string>
